Acceptance criteria:
The selector and generator expose only original Claire and Spiral curls.
Retired IDs fail explicitly before geometry allocation; no disabled/hidden
implementations, prebuilt geometry, resource caches or retired hair GIF files.
Spiral curls contain48 separate swept locks, not merely more samples per lock.
Original waves/motion/material/defaults and opt-in per-view hair stay intact.
Steady playback does not build geometry; caches remain bounded and replaced
buffers are deleted. More selected curls necessarily cost more geometry.
FaceMesh alone has bright red pupils with a smooth local glow, following gaze
and XYZ and occluded by depth; no solid colored facial surface or global bloom.
Mechanical optical design has a bright core, three concentric rings,24 radial
spokes and dark gaps. Keep red, explicitly selected by the owner over blue/cyan.
Other views and Claire Colors retain their intended behavior.
README starts with only a huge centered transparent FaceMesh speaking directly
to the reader, before even its title. All other content is inside one details
section closed by default, including the separate signed XYZ-turning GIF.
Keep the gallery GIF-heavy and showcase only the two available hairstyles.
The main loop includes the owner's fictional horror introduction, real explicit
happy/angry/surprised/sad neural inputs and cyan subtitles embedded below the
face in the same GIF frames. Captions follow phrase timing without independent
HTML timers. Emotional/phonetic realism remains separate human acceptance.
Record exact capture/source hashes and alpha/dimension/timing checks.
Do not begin new snaps/GIF capture or README redesign until owner review/approval.
Do not rewrite Git history, releases, prior qualification receipts or evidence.
No automatic user-runtime restart, sibling/device/profile access or new dependency.

